1965
01:59:43,820 --> 01:59:45,620
So much he needed to dance.

1966
01:59:47,080 --> 01:59:49,160
Man, that feels like an age ago now, actually.

1967
01:59:52,060 --> 01:59:53,020
Kenji Matsutani.

1968
01:59:54,740 --> 01:59:57,100
I wish there was just one guy in this team named Bob.

1969
01:59:57,340 --> 01:59:58,060
That's it, just Bob.

1970
02:00:00,990 --> 02:00:02,730
I wonder what Bob would have done.

1971
02:00:12,520 --> 02:00:13,700
Oh, look!

1972
02:00:14,220 --> 02:00:15,480
It's unfrozen now!

1973
02:00:15,880 --> 02:00:19,040
Unless they're showing the time seven years in the past.

1974
02:00:23,600 --> 02:00:24,700
Redagor Tree Sprout!

1975
02:00:24,780 --> 02:00:25,580
My name is Sprout!

1976
02:00:25,960 --> 02:00:27,560
You've saved the land of Hyrule!

1977
02:00:28,480 --> 02:00:30,720
Once again, Link, you proved to be a true hero!

1978
02:00:31,480 --> 02:00:33,300
The one you can always count on!

1979
02:00:35,600 --> 02:00:36,280
Love that.

1980
02:00:37,700 --> 02:00:40,260
Oh, I'm gonna return to all my friends in the forest!

1981
02:00:46,270 --> 02:00:47,110
That's awesome.

1982
02:00:52,020 --> 02:00:53,460
Hey, look, it's just like the intro.

1983
02:00:53,940 --> 02:00:55,780
Except... there's no Link on the horse.

1984
02:01:01,060 --> 02:01:03,760
I guess I did return back in time, so that...

1985
02:01:03,760 --> 02:01:05,600
So wait, do we have multiple timelines here?

1986
02:01:06,120 --> 02:01:09,660
Does this timeline continue and now Epona is running around alone?

1987
02:01:10,660 --> 02:01:11,660
I hope not.

1988
02:01:28,940 --> 02:01:30,200
They're all partying!

1989
02:01:34,610 --> 02:01:36,390
Even the weird people from the town of there.

1990
02:01:39,920 --> 02:01:42,060
Oh my god, look at that!

1991
02:01:42,360 --> 02:01:43,620
The music, man!

1992
02:01:46,700 --> 02:01:47,740
That's great!

1993
02:01:48,760 --> 02:01:50,220
Wait, are they on a flying carpet?

1994
02:01:54,410 --> 02:01:56,090
Then we got the...

1995
02:01:56,680 --> 02:01:57,310
The builders.

1996
02:02:05,560 --> 02:02:06,260
Nice.

1997
02:02:09,460 --> 02:02:11,060
Wow, he is big.

1998
02:02:12,680 --> 02:02:14,580
These guys are still rotating.

1999
02:02:15,440 --> 02:02:17,140
They never stop rotating.

2000
02:02:20,090 --> 02:02:21,110
King Zora.

2001
02:02:22,450 --> 02:02:24,030
And the little troublemaker.

2002
02:02:25,250 --> 02:02:27,110
Forget his name, but...

2003
02:02:27,450 --> 02:02:28,810
I hope he learns his lesson now.

2004
02:02:32,210 --> 02:02:33,470
No more bullying.

2005
02:02:42,090 --> 02:02:42,730
Look!

2006
02:02:42,870 --> 02:02:43,410
The sages!

2007
02:02:49,690 --> 02:02:50,710
Where are they going?

2008
02:02:58,140 --> 02:02:58,780
Haha!

2009
02:03:00,800 --> 02:03:02,020
She's riding him?

2010
02:03:02,560 --> 02:03:04,120
Oh god, that sounded weird.

2011
02:03:04,640 --> 02:03:05,760
But you know what I mean.

2012
02:03:21,920 --> 02:03:22,680
Hold on.

2013
02:03:38,000 --> 02:03:39,240
Oh, you know what?

2014
02:03:42,380 --> 02:03:44,080
We're gonna return to the village.

2015
02:03:44,280 --> 02:03:45,820
And nobody's gonna believe us.

2016
02:03:46,500 --> 02:03:49,400
And that bully is still gonna be bullying saying, Yeah, right.

2017
02:03:59,950 --> 02:04:01,030
And she's gone!

2018
02:04:16,790 --> 02:04:17,350
Dope!

2019
02:04:21,320 --> 02:04:22,220
Great game!

2020
02:04:23,460 --> 02:04:25,440
Man, I wish I played this as a kid.

2021
02:04:29,390 --> 02:04:31,050
So now we're back in time again.

2022
02:04:37,970 --> 02:04:38,530
Wait.

2023
02:04:39,910 --> 02:04:40,410
No.

2024
02:04:41,130 --> 02:04:42,890
We're not repeating history, are we?

2025
02:04:43,170 --> 02:04:44,130
Are we stuck in a loop?

2026
02:04:52,000 --> 02:04:52,500
No.

2027
02:04:52,640 --> 02:04:53,740
We both know what happened, right?

2028
02:05:13,380 --> 02:05:13,880
Awesome.

2029
02:05:15,540 --> 02:05:18,180
I wonder if that ending is, uh...

2030
02:05:18,920 --> 02:05:20,820
Is up for interpretation a little bit.

2031
02:05:21,720 --> 02:05:23,600
On one hand, I'm like, okay.

2032
02:05:23,840 --> 02:05:26,140
They're reunited again in the past, and...

2033
02:05:26,140 --> 02:05:28,100
The future is saved, you know?

2034
02:05:28,380 --> 02:05:29,160
No evil.

2035
02:05:29,680 --> 02:05:30,540
No more evil.

2036
02:05:31,880 --> 02:05:32,360
But...

2037
02:05:33,200 --> 02:05:34,640
On the other hand...

2038
02:05:35,340 --> 02:05:38,200
Does it mean that we're just repeating everything again?

2039
02:05:38,400 --> 02:05:40,000
And we're gonna go through all the evilism?

2040
02:05:41,500 --> 02:05:42,340
I don't know.

2041
02:05:46,430 --> 02:05:48,030
Well, okay, it...

2042
02:05:48,030 --> 02:05:49,110
There's no more here.

2043
02:05:49,310 --> 02:05:49,830
That's the end.

2044
02:05:50,710 --> 02:05:52,710
The screen doesn't switch or anything.

2045
02:05:57,340 --> 02:05:58,080
There it is.

2046
02:05:59,720 --> 02:06:00,460
There it is.

2047
02:06:03,350 --> 02:06:04,070
We did it.

2048
02:06:06,170 --> 02:06:07,170
Can you believe that?

2049
02:06:11,680 --> 02:06:13,700
I had a feeling I was close to the end, though.

2050
02:06:13,860 --> 02:06:15,480
But there was still a lot there at the end.

2051
02:06:17,840 --> 02:06:18,200
Huh?

2052
02:06:24,340 --> 02:06:25,140
Did you hear that?

2053
02:06:27,200 --> 02:06:27,520
What?

2054
02:06:27,520 --> 02:06:29,860
Da-da-da-da-da-da-da-da-da-da-da.

2055
02:06:32,660 --> 02:06:32,980
What?

2056
02:06:33,100 --> 02:06:33,900
I didn't even do anything.

2057
02:06:35,520 --> 02:06:37,980
Is that the game just messing with me at the end here?

2058
02:06:39,580 --> 02:06:41,140
Yeah, I know it's my song, but...

2059
02:06:42,040 --> 02:06:45,820
So what, that song plays after a minute of staying at the end screen?

2060
02:06:46,340 --> 02:06:47,500
Is that an easter egg?

2061
02:06:51,010 --> 02:06:52,110
Can you end the prediction?

2062
02:06:52,270 --> 02:06:53,910
Wait, what prediction do you guys have running?

2063
02:06:54,230 --> 02:06:54,830
Let's see.

2064
02:06:59,990 --> 02:07:00,770
Let's see here.

2065
02:07:04,550 --> 02:07:06,790
Oh, yes, Deathless, Noe Socks.

2066
02:07:07,590 --> 02:07:08,750
Depends when you made this.

2067
02:07:08,890 --> 02:07:11,030
Did I die or not since you made this prediction?

2068
02:07:15,470 --> 02:07:18,330
It must have been before I started the last boss.

2069
02:07:20,310 --> 02:07:21,390
No, I didn't make it.

2070
02:07:23,130 --> 02:07:25,050
It was Deathless after the prediction.

2071
02:07:25,330 --> 02:07:25,850
Oh, okay, okay.

2072
02:07:27,450 --> 02:07:28,930
Okay, so it's... Oh, okay.

2073
02:07:29,130 --> 02:07:29,490
Beautiful.

2074
02:07:30,610 --> 02:07:32,690
So, I, uh... Yes, Deathless.

2075
02:07:35,370 --> 02:07:36,090
There you go.

2076
02:07:36,430 --> 02:07:38,170
Potatoes have been distributed to the people.

2077
02:07:39,690 --> 02:07:40,130
Amazing.

2078
02:07:41,750 --> 02:07:45,790
Guys, I gotta say, I am so surprised at how good this game is.

2079
02:07:46,670 --> 02:07:49,270
I was expecting it to have aged a little poorly.

2080
02:07:49,890 --> 02:07:50,450
You know?

2081
02:07:51,490 --> 02:08:01,570
But after I got over the initial hurdle of the controls, especially switching versions at first, because there was so much input lag with the first version of the game that I played, that it was...

2082
02:08:01,570 --> 02:08:07,730
It was... It would honestly have made so many, uh, situations in this game incredibly difficult.

2083
02:08:07,930 --> 02:08:10,070
Unless, of course, I have gotten used to it, but...

2084
02:08:10,070 --> 02:08:12,290
That switch... I'm so glad I made that switch.

2085
02:08:13,850 --> 02:08:16,590
Made it so much better, and it totally held up.

2086
02:08:18,850 --> 02:08:20,110
Precious games don't wear off.

2087
02:08:20,210 --> 02:08:20,730
Yeah, you're right.

2088
02:08:21,550 --> 02:08:23,990
But I did have a kind of suspicion...

2089
02:08:24,410 --> 02:08:26,030
But I was wrong about that.

2090
02:08:26,670 --> 02:08:27,470
That, uh...

2091
02:08:27,470 --> 02:08:29,730
A lot of people just had roasting the glasses on, you know?

2092
02:08:30,290 --> 02:08:33,910
Like, yeah, you played it as a kid, so therefore it's special to all of you, but...

2093
02:08:33,910 --> 02:08:35,690
No, this game is objectively good.

2094
02:08:36,250 --> 02:08:37,930
It is actually just a great game.

2095
02:08:41,220 --> 02:08:45,880
I think that ending cinematic, uh, where you run down the castle and all that, would have been mind-blowing as a kid.

2096
02:08:47,300 --> 02:08:50,320
Because even now, I'm like, wow, they actually did that on...

2097
02:08:50,320 --> 02:08:51,760
On the N64.

2098
02:08:52,060 --> 02:08:52,300
Wow.

2099
02:08:56,400 --> 02:08:58,280
That's why it's the highest-rated game of all time.

2100
02:08:58,380 --> 02:08:59,060
According to who, though?

2101
02:08:59,400 --> 02:09:00,080
What metric?

2102
02:09:01,340 --> 02:09:02,360
How do you even say that?

2103
02:09:03,520 --> 02:09:04,240
Oh, Metacritic.

2104
02:09:04,560 --> 02:09:05,240
Is that true?

2105
02:09:07,120 --> 02:09:08,040
I'm in ad jail?

2106
02:09:08,180 --> 02:09:09,000
I'm sorry about that.

2107
02:09:10,260 --> 02:09:10,620
Metacritic.

2108
02:09:10,680 --> 02:09:12,060
Oh, I didn't even know that was the highest-rated game.

2109
02:09:12,060 --> 02:09:12,820
It's the highest-rated game of all time.

2110
02:09:13,960 --> 02:09:14,360
Interesting.

2111
02:09:16,840 --> 02:09:19,040
Guys, I have beaten the best game of all time now.

2112
02:09:20,580 --> 02:09:21,900
It only took me...

2113
02:09:21,900 --> 02:09:22,700
How many years?

2114
02:09:22,900 --> 02:09:24,260
To finally get around to doing it.

2115
02:09:26,740 --> 02:09:28,560
Ganon with no subtitle is so threatening.

2116
02:09:28,720 --> 02:09:28,880
Yeah!

2117
02:09:29,280 --> 02:09:30,720
That actually caught me off guard.

2118
02:09:30,840 --> 02:09:31,920
I thought for sure it was done.

2119
02:09:32,840 --> 02:09:34,620
And then that bastard got up again.

2120
02:09:34,740 --> 02:09:35,720
I mean...

2121
02:09:35,720 --> 02:09:37,380
Villains always do that.

2122
02:09:37,720 --> 02:09:39,000
I should have expected it.

2123
02:09:39,940 --> 02:09:40,680
Of course.

2124
02:09:42,060 --> 02:09:43,160
They always get up again.

2125
02:09:45,440 --> 02:09:46,620
Time for Majora's Mask.

2126
02:09:48,260 --> 02:09:50,640
I'm either gonna play that next, or after the next game.

2127
02:09:52,940 --> 02:09:55,540
Maybe I'll play a small game in between, and then...

2128
02:09:55,540 --> 02:09:56,440
Majora's Mask.

2129
02:09:57,560 --> 02:09:58,200
Something different.

2130
02:09:58,340 --> 02:09:59,840
Just to, you know, switch things up a little bit.

2131
02:10:03,850 --> 02:10:05,130
I don't know what it is yet.

2132
02:10:05,130 --> 02:10:06,090
I'm still thinking about it.

2133
02:10:06,090 --> 02:10:07,150
But something short.

2134
02:10:08,350 --> 02:10:09,710
We're talking max...

2135
02:10:09,710 --> 02:10:12,130
Max five hours or so, I am imagining.

2136
02:10:12,970 --> 02:10:13,750
Something like that.

2137
02:10:13,850 --> 02:10:14,570
A small game, yeah.

2138
02:10:17,330 --> 02:10:20,090
I also want to just let this game settle in me a little bit, you know?

2139
02:10:20,210 --> 02:10:20,990
Give it a week or so.

2140
02:10:21,850 --> 02:10:24,730
Just to absorb the experience before I jump into the new game.

2141
02:10:26,970 --> 02:10:27,690
Maybe Limbo.

2142
02:10:27,830 --> 02:10:29,050
Oh, that's a good idea, actually.

2143
02:10:29,370 --> 02:10:30,710
Because I did play Inside, yeah.

2144
02:10:31,430 --> 02:10:33,830
Dude, I am so excited for, uh...

2145
02:10:33,830 --> 02:10:34,750
What, Playdead?

2146
02:10:34,990 --> 02:10:35,970
Is it Playdead?

2147
02:10:36,570 --> 02:10:38,130
Are they the ones that made Limbo?

2148
02:10:40,170 --> 02:10:42,090
I'm wondering what they're cooking up right now.

2149
02:10:42,570 --> 02:10:45,290
Because they've been working on something for quite a while.

2150
02:10:47,710 --> 02:10:49,530
So, what could that be, you know?

2151
02:10:50,610 --> 02:10:51,530
Really interesting.

2152
02:10:52,370 --> 02:10:54,090
Like, we're talking many years.

2153
02:10:54,230 --> 02:10:55,510
At least six years or so.

2154
02:10:58,870 --> 02:10:59,350
Antechamber?

2155
02:10:59,410 --> 02:11:01,130
Oh, that's an idea, I guess.

2156
02:11:01,130 --> 02:11:02,450
That's like a small puzzle game, right?

2157
02:11:06,960 --> 02:11:11,120
I will say, as amazing as Majora's Mask is, it's definitely a crit game.

2158
02:11:11,400 --> 02:11:13,640
You either enjoy it, or it changes your life.

2159
02:11:13,940 --> 02:11:16,560
Either way, it's really good, and you should play it after Ocarina.

2160
02:11:16,920 --> 02:11:22,400
Yeah, I mean, in the span of, sort of, Zelda, I am playing this next, you know?

2161
02:11:23,800 --> 02:11:26,800
Because apparently that's the release order, anyway.

2162
02:11:27,480 --> 02:11:29,520
Majora's Mask after Ocarina of Time.

2163
02:11:29,680 --> 02:11:32,100
What comes after Majora's Mask, guys?

2164
02:11:33,500 --> 02:11:34,840
Like, in the release order.

2165
02:11:36,400 --> 02:11:38,100
Does anyone know off the top of their head?

2166
02:11:39,520 --> 02:11:40,400
Wind Waker?

2167
02:11:40,560 --> 02:11:40,760
Okay.

2168
02:11:43,020 --> 02:11:49,380
What is that other show or game that sounds like Wind Waker, but is really terrible?

2169
02:11:49,460 --> 02:11:50,420
Everyone's hating on it.

2170
02:11:51,820 --> 02:11:53,140
Wind Breaker or something.

2171
02:11:55,060 --> 02:11:57,080
Or Air Maker.

2172
02:11:57,320 --> 02:11:57,980
Something like that.

2173
02:11:57,980 --> 02:11:58,320
I forgot.

2174
02:11:59,660 --> 02:12:03,040
There's some kind of show, I think, that everyone is hating on.

2175
02:12:03,160 --> 02:12:03,720
Like, it's terrible.

2176
02:12:04,360 --> 02:12:05,460
It's not Zelda-related.

2177
02:12:05,460 --> 02:12:07,160
I'm just, you know, thinking of it right now.

2178
02:12:11,350 --> 02:12:12,930
Do you want to know the timeline situation?

2179
02:12:13,090 --> 02:12:14,530
No, I'm just gonna play the games.

2180
02:12:15,870 --> 02:12:17,090
I'll probably figure it out.

2181
02:12:20,990 --> 02:12:22,750
Will you play the 2D Zelda games?

2182
02:12:24,450 --> 02:12:24,930
Perhaps.

2183
02:12:25,710 --> 02:12:27,750
People were saying I should start with Ocarina, though.

2184
02:12:28,730 --> 02:12:30,850
Perhaps the very old ones haven't...

2185
02:12:30,850 --> 02:12:33,370
Or the very old ones haven't aged very well.

2186
02:12:35,350 --> 02:12:37,710
But I know there's a remake of one of them, right?

2187
02:12:39,070 --> 02:12:40,010
Back to the Future.

2188
02:12:42,870 --> 02:12:44,350
Oh yeah, A Link to the Past.

2189
02:12:45,350 --> 02:12:46,530
It did age well, okay.

2190
02:12:46,970 --> 02:12:48,470
Yeah, they made a new version of it.

2191
02:12:49,250 --> 02:12:50,610
With new graphics and all that.

2192
02:12:54,340 --> 02:12:55,680
You'll probably not figure it out.

2193
02:12:55,820 --> 02:12:56,620
It's very convoluted.

2194
02:12:56,720 --> 02:12:58,060
Well, now you're making me want to play it.

2195
02:12:59,940 --> 02:13:02,260
When you say something like that, then I'm doing it.

2196
02:13:05,180 --> 02:13:06,760
No, that's Link's Awakening.

2197
02:13:06,880 --> 02:13:07,440
Oh, okay, okay.

2198
02:13:08,840 --> 02:13:09,960
There's so many Zelda games.

2199
02:13:10,060 --> 02:13:10,700
I don't know.

2200
02:13:16,400 --> 02:13:17,200
It has puzzles.

2201
02:13:17,760 --> 02:13:18,600
I know you like puzzles.

2202
02:13:19,500 --> 02:13:20,940
I mean, I'm okay with puzzles.

2203
02:13:21,240 --> 02:13:22,300
Let me say this, okay?

2204
02:13:22,560 --> 02:13:23,680
When it comes to puzzles.

2205
02:13:24,520 --> 02:13:26,220
I enjoy the puzzles I can solve.

2206
02:13:26,960 --> 02:13:29,180
And that may sound stupid when you say it like that.

2207
02:13:29,820 --> 02:13:34,200
But puzzles that are so convoluted and weird that I can't figure it out, that's not fun for me.

2208
02:13:35,380 --> 02:13:38,460
I don't enjoy suffering for like a thousand hours trying to solve something.

2209
02:13:39,820 --> 02:13:42,540
I like the games that make me feel smart.

2210
02:13:42,760 --> 02:13:44,120
You know, they present a puzzle.

2211
02:13:44,400 --> 02:13:48,840
And it's so well designed that you can figure it out in a reasonable amount of time.

2212
02:13:48,960 --> 02:13:50,020
And when you do, you feel smart.

2213
02:13:50,180 --> 02:13:51,200
You know, you're like, oh, that's cool.

2214
02:13:51,820 --> 02:13:52,600
That's what I like.

2215
02:13:52,920 --> 02:13:54,660
I'm not particularly good at puzzles.

2216
02:13:55,500 --> 02:13:59,080
I don't know why people have this idea that I am good at puzzles.

2217
02:13:59,180 --> 02:13:59,860
Because I'm really not.

2218
02:14:00,680 --> 02:14:03,260
But I do enjoy them when I can figure them out.

2219
02:14:09,060 --> 02:14:10,140
But here's the thing.

2220
02:14:10,600 --> 02:14:14,820
Even if there's puzzles that I can't figure out, but the game is good and I'm having fun, then it doesn't matter.

2221
02:14:15,820 --> 02:14:19,480
The bottom line is, if the game is fun to play, then I'm gonna play it.

2222
02:14:19,820 --> 02:14:19,980
Right?

2223
02:14:25,070 --> 02:14:27,770
That's basically all Zelda's except both NES titles.

2224
02:14:28,430 --> 02:14:31,010
When you say the NES titles, those are the 2D ones, right?

2225
02:14:31,770 --> 02:14:32,990
Nintendo Entertainment System.

2226
